@startuml Desc_Grounding

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam activityDiamondFontSize 11

<style>
' Named node styles instead of the deprecated "#RRGGBB:label;" colour prefix,
' which newer PlantUML rejects in favour of a trailing <<stereotype>>.
' This form renders on both old and new versions.
.found   { BackgroundColor #C8E6C9 }
.slm     { BackgroundColor #FFE0B2 }
.vlm     { BackgroundColor #BBDEFB }
.failure { BackgroundColor #FFCDD2 }
</style>

title desc= locator - tiered grounding over the DOM (ADR-022, ADR-024)\nDescriptionResolver.resolve()

start
:desc="settings button top right"
inputs: current DOM (+ screenshot stored at dump time);
if (per-screen cache hit?) then (yes)
  :return cached result;
  stop
else (no)
endif

partition "Tier 1 - lexical  (no model, always on)" #E8F5E9 {
  :score every element:
  token/synonym overlap vs label / text / hint
  + role words ("button", "field", ...);
  if (confident?\nscore floor AND margin over runner-up) then (yes)
    :element (log: tier=lexical); <<found>>
    stop
  else (no - a tie escalates,\nnever a guess)
  endif
}

:positional words ("top right", "left", ...)?
enforce GEOMETRICALLY on the candidate set
- never delegated to a model;
note right
  a 3B model confidently called a
  top-left element "top right" -
  position is deterministic geometry
end note

partition "Tier 2 - SLM over DOM  (if configured)" #FFF3E0 {
  :compact element table (id | role | text | label | position)
  -> small text LM, temperature 0
  -> returns an element id;
  if (id exists in the DOM?) then (no)
    :reject - hallucinated id;
  else (yes)
    :element (log: tier=slm); <<slm>>
    stop
  endif
}

partition "Tier 3 - VLM Set-of-Mark  (opt-in)" #E3F2FD {
  :number the candidate boxes ON THE STORED SCREENSHOT
  -> vision model picks a number
  (no re-capture, no coordinate regression);
  if (confident pick?) then (yes)
    :element - a real DOM element\nBY CONSTRUCTION (log: tier=vlm); <<vlm>>
    stop
  else (no)
  endif
}

:FAIL LOUDLY:\n"no grounding tier confident\n(nearest: E1, E10, E23, ...)"; <<failure>>
stop

legend bottom
  **Ambiguity arbitration (ADR-024 v1.1):** when a property locator
  (text=+) matches SEVERAL elements and the chain has a desc=, the same
  resolver runs restricted to just those candidates (within=...) -
  a 2-3 element pool is where every tier is most reliable.
  Every escalated hit logs which tier answered.
end legend

@enduml
